{"id": "EUVD-2026-28720", "enisaUuid": "84b95c44-61d8-3c25-9e62-933f57d0f897", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: qla2xxx: Completely fix fcport double free\n\nIn qla24xx_els_dcmd_iocb() sp->free is set to qla2x00_els_dcmd_sp_free().\nWhen an error happens, this function is called by qla2x00_sp_release(),\nwhen kref_put() releases the first and the last reference.\n\nqla2x00_els_dcmd_sp_free() frees fcport by calling qla2x00_free_fcport().\nDoing it one more time after kref_put() is a bad idea.", "datePublished": "2026-05-08T14:21:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:40:46", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/baabbd29191514391ca81594e43261bd17c6795a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7172f41786dc08144da4627483e405de57bf8d2c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4097a2afe8acc6038b71aab825430f1403decf20", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d48ea85463f5b34f7b92ea0a13eddf1ab993da7b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c0b7da13a04bd70ef6070bfb9ea85f582294560a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-43414", "GHSA-qm6r-96cc-q36w"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05aee19b-f45f-3594-99c5-ab7231b5227b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cd10dee1f07a782f5aa05703c55299ca86a85ee4"}, {"id": "1337bd0d-f8b5-381c-bc7a-51b962c4c65f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f85af9f1aa5e2f53694a6cbe72010f754b5ff862"}, {"id": "23afa2c7-616e-3129-91e4-c32108457487", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2622536b-47f5-3808-9a91-725be0ce3b55", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "2b13be82-f722-37f3-8d0c-f03a06e5050d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version":